.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt VV 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vv
.Nd print a tool version as a strict SemVer triple
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar tool
.Pp
.Nm
.Fl -verified-version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints exactly one
.Li X.Y.Z
line for
.Ar tool .
Missing or unparseable versions produce
.Li 0.0.0 .
Normal lookups always exit zero.
.Pp
Lookup prefers a valid upstream
.Fl -verified-version
response unless the command is known to handle unknown options unsafely.
It then uses a known compatibility fallback or
.Ar tool
.Fl -version .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -verified-version , Fl -version
Print the
.Nm
version.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print brief help.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width VV_TIMEOUT
.It Ev VV_TIMEOUT
Probe timeout in seconds. Default: 5.
.El
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
Known command exceptions are built into
.Nm .
They control whether probing is safe, which fallback arguments are used, and
whether useful output may accompany a non-zero exit.
There are no user recipe or parser configuration files.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The utility exits zero for every normal result, including missing or
unparseable tools. Invalid options exit two. Any other non-zero status
indicates a defect in
.Nm .
